<title>USA: Marathon cuts US posted crude prices 50 cts.</title>
<headline>Marathon cuts US posted crude prices 50 cts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marathon Oil Corp, a unit of USX-Marathon Group, said it had lowered the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 50 cents, effective Friday.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $18.50 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $16.90 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $18.75 and Oklahoma sweet is $18.50.</p>
</text>
